# --- s020 Book I d.3 q.5 (= Ord. I d.3 p.2 q. un., nn. 281–332: the vestigium)
n("n388","s020-01","Quinta questio tertie distinctionis","la","commentary","= *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 2 q. un. (Vatican III, nn. 281–332), *utrum in qualibet creatura sit vestigium Trinitatis*. Gorris omits *qualibet*. His first argument is Scotus's n. 281, verbatim.","verified")
n("n389","s020-01","Aug. 6°. de trini. c. vlti.","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* VI 10.12, quoted after *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 284 (*VI De Trinitate cap. ultimo*). A *quodammodo* for Scotus's *quomodo* is a misreading of the exemplar.","verified")
n("n390","s020-02","opinio Thome primo scripti di. 3. articulo. 2°.","la","source","Thomas, *In I Sent.* d. 3 q. 2 a. 1 (*vestigium… impressio derelicta ex transitu alicuius*). The definition is given anonymously by Scotus at *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 286. Gorris supplies the attribution and the passage (his 'article 2' is the Parma *quaestio* 2).","certain")
n("n391","s020-02","ipsum in parte representans","la","textual","Scotus (n. 286) has *ipsum imperfecte repraesentans*. Gorris (and B) *in parte* is a gloss rather than a variant.","certain")
n("n392","s020-02","opinio Henrici quodlibeto. 9. q. 1. et. 2.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* IX qq. 1–2, on the threefold or twofold relation of creature to God. The opinion is reported anonymously at *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 287 (three relations, to God as triple cause, according to the three modes of relatives in *Metaph.* V).","to-verify")
n("n393","s020-02","in ratitudine rei. sed in aliquiditate tantum","la","source","Henry's distinction of *ratitudo* and *aliquitas* (*Ord.* I d. 3 nn. 302–309, where Scotus reports that *quo aliquid est dicitur 'ratitudo'… 'quid' dicitur 'aliquitas'*). Henry's *Quodl.* III q. 9, V q. 2, IV qq. 7–8 and II q. 3 are the loci Gorris gives. Note that Gorris reverses the thesis as Scotus reports it: for Henry the creature's *ratitudo* *is* its relation to God, founded on its *aliquitas*.","to-verify")
n("n394","s020-03","sunt tria videnda","la","commentary","Gorris re-labels Scotus's three articles (n. 285) as the 'Doctor's' own three points. Of Scotus's critical replies he keeps only the definition of the trace (n. 293), the doctrine of *unitas–species–ordo* (n. 298) and the appropriations (n. 299–301). He passes over in silence Scotus's long attack on Henry's *ratitudo* (nn. 310–323).","certain")
n("n395","s020-04","non pro⟨prie re⟩presentaret bouem","la","textual","A has a stain at the top right of p. 36. B reads *non ꝓ̄* | *representaret* at a line-break. I take B's abbreviation as *proprie* and conjecture A *pro⟨prie re⟩presentaret*. Cf. *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 293: *si pes amputatus a corpore imprimeret vestigium*.","conjecture")
n("n396","s020-04","vt ymago iouis representans iouem","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 286: *imago Iovis non repraesentat Caesarem*.","verified")
n("n397","s020-05","hec omnia que arte diuina facta sunt","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* VI 10.12 (*Haec igitur omnia quae arte divina facta sunt, et unitatem quandam in se ostendunt, et speciem, et ordinem*), as at *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 298. *In illa Trinitate summa origo est rerum omnium* is from the same chapter, also quoted by Scotus.","verified")
n("n398","s020-05","nam vult quod ista primo fundentur in absolutis","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 298: *nec in solis respectibus consistit vestigium sed in aliquibus absolutis*.","verified")
n("n399","s020-05","nam beatitudo est summa dilectio","la","commentary","Gorris's own gloss linking *ordo* (in Augustine's sense of the will's ordered love) to beatitude as supreme love. Not in Scotus here.","certain")
n("n400","s020-06","propriatorum anime","la","textual","So A. The sense requires *appropriatorum*. *anime* is hard to construe: perhaps 'appropriated [by] the soul', i.e. in our way of conceiving. Check against B.","uncertain")
n("n401","s020-07","Trinitas est quoddam totum numerabile","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 301 (*Trinitas est quasi quoddam totum numerale, saltem in conceptu intellectus, persona autem ibi est quasi pars totius huius*), almost verbatim.","verified")
n("n402","s020-07","non distincte sed indistincte","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 330.","verified")
n("n403","s020-06","appropriated by the soul","en","translation","A *propriatorum anime*. The rendering is tentative. See note on the Latin.","uncertain")
# --- B collation (full): B33L–B34L
n("n1094","s020-01","cuius in creatura quodammodo","la","textual","B: *Cum in creatura quodammodo*. A's *cuius* is Augustine's reading.","certain")
upd("n392", append=" B omits everything from *quodlibeto. 9. q. 1. et. 2.* to the second *opinio Henrici* (homoeoteleuton) and reads *ponitur opinio Henrici quolibet. iij. q. ix.* … It therefore assigns to the second article the references that A gives to the third.")
n("n1095","s020-03","in quo existit","la","textual","B: *in quo consistat*.","certain")
n("n1096","s020-04","et per figuram pedis","la","textual","B: *vt per figuram pedis*. B's *vt* gives the needed sense, and the translation follows it.","certain")
n("n1097","s020-04","as from the shape","en","translation","A reads *et per figuram*. The translation follows B's *vt*.")
upd("n400", append=" B reads *respectu proprietatem anime*, perhaps for *proprietatum anime* ('with respect to the properties of the soul'). This does not settle the reading.")
upd("n401", append=" B: *Trinitas est quoddam totum immateriale saltem respectu intellectus nostri*. A's *numerabile … in conceptu* is closer to Scotus.")
n("n1098","s020-07","nec tantum hoc sed appropriabile","la","textual","B: *nec tantum hoc est appropriabile*.","certain")
